From: nxrs contributors
Subject: [PATCH] xtensa: use the compiler wchar_t minimum when available

GCC 16 defines a 16-bit unsigned wchar_t and __WCHAR_MIN__=0 on ESP32-S3,
but does not define __WCHAR_UNSIGNED__. Prefer its explicit minimum so
WCHAR_MIN matches the actual type. Keep the existing older-compiler fallbacks.

Source: 4268617f28ad0ed7e900a081ea1b33c9347458b3

--- a/arch/xtensa/include/limits.h
+++ b/arch/xtensa/include/limits.h
@@ -73,6 +73,9 @@
 #if !defined(__WCHAR_TYPE__)
 #  define WCHAR_MIN INT_MIN
 #  define WCHAR_MAX INT_MAX
+#elif defined(__WCHAR_MIN__)
+#  define WCHAR_MIN __WCHAR_MIN__
+#  define WCHAR_MAX __WCHAR_MAX__
 #elif defined(__WCHAR_UNSIGNED__)
 #  define WCHAR_MIN 0
 #  define WCHAR_MAX __WCHAR_MAX__
